Guard deployments against the wrong deployer.

A deployer image can be run against a configuration naming other
images, or a host a newer deployer has changed. Each deploy now records
its deployer on each host, and checks refuse a deployer for an older
release than a host's record, or an upgrade upstream does not support.

The rules are in a filter plugin so that they are unit tested. Only a
deployer image knows its release, so a virtualenv writes the record but
is not checked. destroy.yml is never checked, so that a mistake can
always be cleaned up.

